{"name":"Pocket Watch","hex":"#c2a781","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pocket watch","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A watch carried in the pocket, often with a closing cover and usually attached to a chain."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To jealously obsess over another person's finances or success."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pocket_watch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pocket watch","blocks":[{"text":"A pocket watch is a watch that is made to be carried in a pocket, as opposed to a wristwatch, which is strapped to the wrist."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Pocket_Watch_%28Savonette%29.jpg/330px-Pocket_Watch_%28Savonette%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pocket_watch","wikidata":"Q849813"},{"title":"Pocket","blocks":[{"text":"A pocket is a small bag- or envelope-shaped compartment that is either sewn into or attached to clothing, designed for carrying small items. Pockets are also found on luggage, backpacks, and similar containers. Historically, the term could also refer to a separate pouch or small bag."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Jeans_pocket_back.jpg/330px-Jeans_pocket_back.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pocket","wikidata":"Q321767"},{"title":"Watch","blocks":[{"text":"A watch is a timepiece carried or worn by a person. It is designed to maintain a consistent movement despite the motions caused by the person's activities. A wristwatch is worn around the wrist, attached by a watch strap or another type of bracelet, including metal bands or leather straps. A pocket watch is carried in a pocket, often attached to a chain. A stopwatch is a type of watch that measures intervals of time."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Rolex_Oyster_Perpetual_with_a_%22Jubliee%22_dial.jpg/330px-Rolex_Oyster_Perpetual_with_a_%22Jubliee%22_dial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watch","wikidata":"Q178794"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/MontreGousset001.jpg/500px-MontreGousset001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/MontreGousset001.jpg/500px-MontreGousset001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A golden pocket watch with hunter-case and watch chain","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMontreGousset001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Henlein_Taschenuhr.jpg/500px-Henlein_Taschenuhr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Henlein_Taschenuhr.jpg/1280px-Henlein_Taschenuhr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Henlein_Taschenuhr.jpg/500px-Henlein_Taschenuhr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pocket watches evolved from clock-watches, supposedly called Nuremberg eggs, worn on chains around the neck. Example by Peter Henlein, 1510, Germanisches Nationalmuseum Nuremberg.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHenlein_Taschenuhr.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Pocketwatch_movement.png/500px-Pocketwatch_movement.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Pocketwatch_movement.png/500px-Pocketwatch_movement.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Antique verge fusée pocket watch movement, 